<blockquote>
<p>The chamber is affixed with a satellite-synchronized 24-hour clock set to Greenwich Mean Time. The coin is secured centrally within a free-spinning armature, both ends of which are held in place by way of magnetic levitation to assure against friction.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These procedures seem unnecessary and are detracting to me. The video cameras can record the time of events, and I don't understand the need to carefully suspend the coin.</p>
