<p>Ditto. I was with you until that line, but then I hit it and had to downvote. &quot;Destiny&quot; isn't a word that should be used in a document like this, because it's meaningless in a scientific sense. Predestination requires that the universe be deterministic, which has not, to my knowledge, been actually proven. And, in fact, I have no idea what that sentence <em>means</em>, if there's no causal or predictive relationship between the coin and the event. Are you trying to say that it's the event that causes the coin to flip and not the other way around?</p>

